  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Activity under preparation Green Value for Growth</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Mozambique&#xbf;s growth heavily relies on extractive sectors, with little diversification and value addition, and a resulting limited capacity to address job creation and poverty reduction. Higher productivity agriculture and the development of the agro-industry, will be vital to generate economic opportunities and achieve a more inclusive growth path. However, agriculture intensification and value chains development often fail to handle their social, economic and environmental trade-offs, setting a harmful cycle of ecosystems&#xbf; degradation and increased poverty and vulnerability. The proposed Action seeks to enhance nature positive value chains, promoting resilient and productive landscapes and fostering entrepreneurship and SMEs growth, ultimately supporting Mozambique&#xbf;s transition towards greener, more climate resilient and inclusive growth. The Action will focus on a limited number of agroforestry and crop value chains such as cashew, avocado and soy, along strategic corridors selected for their projected contribution to sustainable agri-food systems, job creation and a thriving private sector.</narrative>
  </description>
